IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nt-part1-application`

-- Tests of nt-part1-application.l4.
-- Every expected value is written from the text of the section named beside it.

§ `Section 2(3)`

-- All three conditions met: the provision in the earlier law continues to apply.
#ASSERT `s 2(3): the provision of the earlier law continues to apply to the word, expression or provision` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Each condition failing on its own: the subsection does not operate.
#ASSERT `s 2(3): the provision of the earlier law continues to apply to the word, expression or provision` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(3): the provision of the earlier law continues to apply to the word, expression or provision` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(3): the provision of the earlier law continues to apply to the word, expression or provision` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 2(4)`

#ASSERT `s 2(4): reference is made to the law in force when the thing was done or suffered, and not to this Act` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Outside the scope of the subsection the text does not say.
#ASSERT `s 2(4): reference is made to the law in force when the thing was done or suffered, and not to this Act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(4): reference is made to the law in force when the thing was done or suffered, and not to this Act` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 3(1)`

#ASSERT `s 3(1): this Act applies to the law as though the law were an Act` `an Act of the Legislative Assembly` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1): this Act applies to the law as though the law were an Act` `an Ordinance of the Northern Territory` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1): this Act applies to the law as though the law were an Act` `an Ordinance of the State of South Australia in its application to the Northern Territory` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1): this Act applies to the law as though the law were an Act` `an Act of the State of South Australia in its application to the Northern Territory` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Subject to section 2.
#ASSERT `s 3(1): this Act applies to the law as though the law were an Act` `an Act of the Legislative Assembly` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(1): this Act applies to the law as though the law were an Act` `an Ordinance of the Northern Territory` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A law of some other kind is not among those listed.
#ASSERT `s 3(1): this Act applies to the law as though the law were an Act` `a law of some other kind` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(1): this Act applies to the law as though the law were an Act` `a law of some other kind` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 3(2)`

#ASSERT `s 3(2): this Act binds the Crown in the capacity` `the Crown in right of the Territory` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(2): this Act binds the Crown in the capacity` `the Crown in right of the Territory` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(2): this Act binds the Crown in the capacity` `the Crown in some other capacity` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- So far as the legislative power does not permit, the text does not say.
#ASSERT `s 3(2): this Act binds the Crown in the capacity` `the Crown in some other capacity` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 3(3)`

#ASSERT `s 3(3): the provision of this Act yields to the other provision` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(3): the provision of this Act yields to the other provision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 4`

#ASSERT `s 4: the way in which this Act applies to the thing` `a statutory instrument made under a law to which this Act applies` TRUE EQUALS JUST `as if the instrument were an Act`
#ASSERT `s 4: the way in which this Act applies to the thing` `the interpretation, application and effect of such an instrument` TRUE EQUALS JUST `as if the instrument were an Act`
#ASSERT `s 4: the way in which this Act applies to the thing` `a reference to a statutory instrument` TRUE EQUALS JUST `as if the reference to the instrument were a reference to an Act`
#ASSERT `s 4: the way in which this Act applies to the thing` `a reference to an Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST `as if the reference to an Act were a reference to such an instrument`
-- "So far as it is applicable": where it is not applicable the text does not say.
#ASSERT `s 4: the way in which this Act applies to the thing` `a statutory instrument made under a law to which this Act applies` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4: the way in which this Act applies to the thing` `a reference to an Act` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4: the way in which this Act applies to the thing` `a thing of some other kind` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4: the way in which this Act applies to the thing` `a thing of some other kind` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
